      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settled in 1757, Wyoming saw early industrial activity thanks to the hydropower provided by the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyoming%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Brand's Iron Works operated on the Hopkinton side of the river by 1787 in Wyoming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyoming%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Brothers Cotton Mill was established on the Richmond side of Wyoming in 1814.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyoming%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A tavern was established in 1815 on the Richmond side of the river to serve travelers on the New London Turnpike.",
